//! Pump-action: a 12 V controller that empties a tank.
//!
//! Two float switches watch the tank. When the top one closes (tank full) the pump starts and
//! stays on, latched, while the level falls. When the bottom one closes (tank empty) the pump
//! keeps running for an adjustable time `T` (1 to 25 s, one pot) and then stops. It stays off
//! while the tank refills, although the bottom float is closed at the start of the refill.
//!
//! One NE555 does both jobs, latch and timer, straight from the 12 V rail:
//!
//! | Namespace    | What it holds                                                        |
//! | ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |
//! | `parts`      | resistor, capacitor, diode, supply, pot, a switch closed by a `Bit`  |
//! | `ne555`      | the timer IC: divider, two comparators, latch, output, discharge     |
//! | `relay`      | coil (R + L) and a contact with pick-up / drop-out hysteresis        |
//! | `controller` | `PumpAction`: the board, wired exactly as the schematic in README.md |
//!
//! The pump, the floats and the tank are the outside world: `Pump` is here because every bench
//! needs one, the tank lives in `benches/cycle.msl`.

pub mod parts;

pub mod ne555;

pub mod relay;

pub mod controller;

pub use crate::controller::{PumpAction, Pump};
